# Autonomous AEP execution (when mandated)

Use the user's requested outcome and the authority granted in the host `AGENTS.md` or
`governance/LOCAL_OVERLAY.md`. A natural-language request to deliver an outcome or
finish an authorized AEP, wave, or task list is sufficient (e.g. “fix this behavior”,
“udělej všechny body z AEP”).

## Triggers (non-exhaustive)

References to the active AEP, execution ledger, wave packages, or `specs/*/tasks.md`.
An ordinary request to deliver a result also qualifies. For an analysis-only or plan-only
request, the requested analysis or plan is the deliverable.

## After each milestone and before ending the turn

Compare the original requested outcome with what the current evidence actually covers.
For an unmet criterion, choose and perform the next authorized action in this turn.
If the next action is unclear, inspect a relevant caller, test, log or project decision.
Use the finding to choose and execute a supporting step. Update the plan if one is in use.
Continue independent work if one step is blocked. Finish when the whole outcome is
verified, the user stops the run, or every remaining route has a concrete blocker
under the host mandate or budget. Report the evidence and any decision still needed.

## What to do

1. Read the host mandate (`AGENTS.md`, overlay) and any task record already in use
   (for example `docs/EXECUTION_STATE.md`, `specs/*/progress.md`, or a cited AEP).
   When the task needs an AEP, form it using the host's existing readiness rules.
2. For a plan with remaining steps and the procedure pin available, execute inline per
   `vendor/superpowers/v7.0.2/skills/executing-plans/SKILL.md`.
3. Route debugging, TDD, and completion checks through other pinned Superpowers under
   `vendor/superpowers/v7.0.2/skills/` — same routing as
   `.cursor/skills/governed-work/SKILL.md`, without requiring that skill to be invoked.
4. When the task uses a host ledger, update it on each meaningful slice.
5. Ambiguity: decide from spec/plan; log `Ruling:` in the ledger; collect
   `Open questions (post-run)` — do not block the chain unless every path is a guess
   (AEP BLOCKED).
6. Respect the host's decision points for sensitive actions, irreversible effects,
   merge/push/deploy, missing inputs and exhausted repair budgets. Identify the
   specific action that is blocked and the evidence or decision needed to proceed.
7. Before push or merge, record acceptance with `ci/run_task_acceptance_check.sh`
   when that wrapper exists. A green git hook is not that record. Tier C does not
   sandbox the agent shell; downloads into a gitignored tool root need an explicit mandate.

Spec Kit `review-spec` / `review-plan` gates do not apply to authorized wave work unless
the operator asked for a review stop.

Customize paths and ADR references in this file after copy if your project uses different
ledger or mandate locations.
